## 5. Documentation, skill and compatibility surfaces

- New: one command, one API function (ninth function, twelfth `__all__` name,
  appended), one schema, one reference page, one how-to, one example.
- No change to the `check`, `witness` or `replay` contracts.
- Release note in WN2, with the surface (`compatibility.md:7`). (p1-I)
- Packaged skills: WN3-C4.

## 6. Risks and required controls

| Risk | Control |
|---|---|
| Why-not and `check` disagree | WN-R2 status-first design; WN1 T8 over the whole corpus |
| An unavailable relation read as empty | WN-R2; T8 cases for target, positive dependency, negated dependency, descent target |
| Declared order misleads when the evaluator reorders | `"order": "declared"` in the payload; a corpus case where the orders differ |
| Unbounded work in the pre-evaluation or in probes | WN-R4; charge-only trace; counter tests (WN1-C5) |
| Values leak | WN-R5 closed view; WN2-C2 leak test |
| "Blocked" read as "false" | Docs state why-not explains a missing derivation in this population; it proves nothing about the world |
| The oracle shares code with the kernel | Oracle imports nothing from `gnd.extensions`, `gnd.terms` or `gnd.values` |
| Downstream names leak | WN-R8 denylist test; review lens |
| A repair round introduces defects | §8 round budget and stop rule |

## 7. Out of scope

- A field in the `check` report or any report schema bump.
- The direct-derivation request (GR-T5) and the reporter's other requests.
- Automatic repair: GND names the gap; adding facts is the host's move.
- Partially bound descent (WN-D3).
- Explaining constraint violations (already reported by `check`).
- Aggregates and opaque rules; native, LQP and PyRel runtimes.
- Changes inside the downstream application. Publication, release,
  certification.

## 8. Execution, approval and review protocol

`auto=false`. Each phase follows `process-phase`: spec, owner gate,
implementation and focused tests, an independent diff review, a refactoring
review and a record. No code is written before recorded spec approval. Plan and
close review: four local readers, WN-D8 `(o)`, with lenses: correctness against
production semantics; implementability; protocol and anonymity; test design and
falsifiability. The per-phase diff instrument is **proposed**: one local reader
per phase. (p1-K) One reader is one reader, not a panel.

Round budget: round 1 ran over r1. One confirmation round runs over r2, limited
to the blocking themes (A, B, C, D, I, J). Then the stop rule from
`review-convergence.md` applies. No third round without a new owner request.
Work happens on a topic branch, then a PR; merge requires the owner.

## 9. Per-phase verification story

| Phase | Expected result | Focused gate (p1-K) |
|---|---|---|
| WN1 | Kernel agrees with production and the oracle; counters fix outcomes; no public diff | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_why_not_kernel.py tests/test_why_not_oracle.py tests/test_rf1_layering.py tests/test_rf4_peripheral.py tests/test_rf6_query_policy.py tests/test_gnd_arch.py tests/test_public_v71_witness_corpus.py tests/test_public_optional_value_witness.py` |
| WN2 | Goldens pass; schema validates; pins updated; check/witness parity | WN1 gate plus `tests/test_public_why_not.py tests/test_public_api.py tests/test_v61_phase2_api.py tests/test_public_reference_signatures.py tests/test_rf1_cli_pins.py tests/test_rf5_commands.py tests/test_rf5_handler_pins.py tests/test_documentation_tutorials.py`; `test_public_built_inventory.py` and `test_public_runtime.py` are distribution lanes, run on owner selection |
| WN3 | Two-gap repair loop passes; docs build | WN2 gate plus the example test and the installed-docs check |

The broad suite runs on explicit owner selection.

## 10. Owner decisions and open questions

| ID | Question | Readings and cost | Ruling or proposal |
|---|---|---|---|
| WN-D1 | Surface | (a) new command + API in the witness lane; (b) a `check` report field: schema bump, cost on every check; (c) both | proposed **(a)** |
| WN-D2 | Which order defines "first blocking atom" | (a) declaration-order prefixes: readable, can enumerate a product (exit 4 sooner); (b) the evaluator's reordered join: cheaper, but the "first" atom depends on connectivity | proposed **(a)**, order named in the payload |
| WN-D3 | Descent into a derived blocker | (a) none; (b) ground atoms only, cycles keyed on (predicate, row); (c) partially bound descent: a new pattern mode | **(b)** `(p1, adopted)` |
| WN-D4 | Values in output | (a) API raw like `api.witness`, CLI redacted with `--raw`; (b) `unredacted=False` like `check`: API redacted by default, a third spelling for the lane; (c) a new `raw=False`: a fourth convention | **(a)** `(p1, adopted)` |
| WN-D5 | Exit bands | (a) r1: `0` blocked, `2` derived or unsupported: host cannot tell them apart; (b) `0` blocked or derived (read `status`), `2` unsupported, `3`, `4` unavailable or work limit | **(b)** `(p1, adopted)` |
| WN-D6 | Fragment and ceilings | fragment as §2; ceilings in a sibling `WhyNotLimits` (WitnessLimits values plus a `probes` field) rather than widening `WitnessLimits`, which witness's `checked_limits` iterates | proposed as stated (p1-C) |
| WN-D7 | Code home | (a) `gnd.witness.why_not`; (b) a new lane | proposed **(a)** |
| WN-D8 | Review instrument for plan and close | | **Ruled (o) 2026-10-30:** four local readers |
| WN-D9 | Sample count | | proposed 5, total count always given |
| WN-D10 | Approval instrument per phase | WN1 prose: its payload is internal and WN2 fixes the wire form; WN2 corpus-first: it ships a serialized format, exit codes and refusals (`review-convergence.md`) | proposed as stated (p1-K) |
| WN-D11 | Rows per call | (a) one row matching `--fact-type`, else exit 3; (b) many rows with a combining rule: a host loop asks per claim anyway | proposed **(a)** |
| WN-D12 | Schema home and vendoring | (a) `src/gnd/why-not.schema.json`, no skill copy; (b) `src/gnd/schema/` beside the witness schemas, which mixes output with synced interchange schemas; (c) also vendor into `gnd-export/references` with a sync test and two `EXPECTED_SKILL_FILES` pins | proposed **(a)** |
| WN-D13 | The stale ten-name tuple in `test_public_runtime.py:52` | (a) fix it in WN2 to the twelve names, recorded; (b) leave it: a distribution probe that would then be two names behind | proposed **(a)** |

No open question is inherited from an earlier milestone.
